The  program provides information on System V interprocess commu‐
nication (IPC) facilities on the system.  The options are as fol‐
lows: Show the maximum amount of information possible  when  dis‐
playing active semaphores, message queues, and shared memory seg‐
ments.  (This is shorthand for specifying the and options.)  Show
the  maximum allowed sizes for active semaphores, message queues,
and shared memory segments.  The is the maximum number  of  bytes
in a message on a message queue, the size of a shared memory seg‐
ment,  or  the number of semaphores in a set of semaphores.  Show
the creator’s name  and  group  for  active  semaphores,  message
queues,  and  shared  memory segments.  Display information about
active shared memory segments.  Show outstanding usage for active
message queues, and shared memory segments.  The is the number of
messages in a message queue, or the number of processes  attached
to  a shared memory segment.  Show the process ID information for
active semaphores, message queues, and  shared  memory  segments.
The is the last process to send a message to or receive a message
from  a  message  queue, the process that created a semaphore, or
the last process to attach or detach  a  shared  memory  segment.
Display  information about active message queues.  Display infor‐
mation about active semaphores.  Show  access  times  for  active
semaphores,  message queues, and shared memory segments.  The ac‐
cess times is the time of the last control operation  on  an  IPC
object, the last send or receive of a message, the last attach or
detach  of  a  shared  memory segment, or the last operation on a
semaphore.  Display system information about shared memory.  Dis‐
play system information about messages  queues.   Display  system
information  about  semaphores.  Display system information about
shared memory, message queues and semaphores.  (This is shorthand
for specifying the and options.)  If none of the or  options  are
specified, information about all active IPC facilities is listed.
